theorem two-halves-below
  note        Adding A < C/2 and B < C/2 gives A + B < C/2 + C/2, which is C.
  let A ∈ ℝ                                                           (H1)
  let B ∈ ℝ                                                           (H2)
  let C ∈ ℝ                                                           (H3)
  assume A < C/2                                                      (H4)
  assume B < C/2                                                      (H5)
  then A + B < C

1.  A + B < C
    inequalities, from H4, H5
